#X text 12 1420 scopes: opl3~ chip channels 1-18 (outlets 2-19 \, three per row \, pan-independent per-channel capture - a channel silenced by its C0 pan bits still shows here) and the log's DAC PCM stream (bottom left \, vgm~ outlet 2 \, linear-interpolated at the logged write times);
#X text 12 1462 the two sums (left / right \, not scoped) go through their own gains into dac~ - NOT one multiplier fed both outlets: that multiplies left BY right \, and pan-split notes vanish wherever the other channel is quiet;
#X text 12 1520 outlet 0 of vgm~ = the YM2612 register stream (see vgm-player.pd) \, outlet 3 = end bang. One patch can host the whole rig - each outlet feeds its own chip;
